<!--
  Golden file for WP2/WP6/WP7 (ERSAD NeTEx export).
  Source: Confluence page 3825765495 "ERSAD Export aus ATLAS", the three-station example
  (Burgdorf 8508005, Yverdon-les-Bains 8504200, Bellinzona 8505213).

  Adaptations applied vs. the Confluence draft, per plan section 0.2:
  1. No Parking/ParkingArea/TotalCapacity elements exist in this example, so nothing to remove
     there.
  2. No separate "prmTsiCompliantStation" element existed in the draft; not derivable from ATLAS
     data and omitted entirely (known limitation).
  3. Coordinates are already WGS84 decimal degrees in the source; no conversion needed for this
     golden file's literal values.
  4. Markdown backslash-escapes ("STOP\_POINT", "NOT\_APPLICABLE" etc.) introduced by the
     Confluence-to-markdown export were unescaped back to plain XML comment text.

  This example has no Contact Point, Parking Lot, Reference Point or SitePathLink data (per the
  spec: "fuer nicht in den beigelegten Beispiel-Exporten vorhandene ... werden bewusst keine Werte
  erfunden"), so it does not exercise ErsadParking/ErsadContactPoint/ErsadPathLink at all -
  see tavannes-8500100.xml for those.

  WP6 adaptations (StAX writer is the element contract; plan section 0.2 wins over the draft):
  5. Added xmlns:gml / xmlns:siri declarations to the root element (plan WP6 header).
  6. Removed the Burgdorf toilet <Note> ("Im Lokal Spetaccolo ..."): the ERSAD toilet model has no
     free-text info field.
  7. Yverdon-les-Bains and Bellinzona (accessibility = PRE_REGISTRATION): StopPlace
     MobilityImpairedAccess and WheelchairAccess changed from "true" to "partial" (section 0.2:
     PRE_REGISTRATION maps to partial).

  Handoff plan Section 8 / schema-validity follow-up (this revision):
  8. (8.4) Quay AccessVehicleEquipment id suffix renamed ":boarding" -> ":access" everywhere.
  9. (8.3, known limitation, no longer exported) Removed all Quay &lt;TactileGuidingStrips&gt;
     (was sourced from platform contrastingAreas) and StopPlace &lt;VisualSignsAvailable&gt;
     (was sourced from visualInfo) at every station.
  10. (8.1) Quay AccessVehicleEquipment rebuilt using real AccessVehicleEquipmentBoardingGroup
      elements (Hoist/Ramp; LIFTS maps to true Hoist, RAMPS maps to true Ramp, NO maps to false,
      else omitted; written only if Hoist or Ramp is present): Burgdorf and Bellinzona quays all
      have boardingDevice TO_BE_COMPLETED, so none write AccessVehicleEquipment anymore
      (previously every quay wrote BoardingHeightAdjustment, which does not exist in NeTEx).
      Yverdon quay :0:619346 (boardingDevice = RAMPS) now writes Ramp=true; the other Yverdon
      quays (TO_BE_COMPLETED / NOT_APPLICABLE) write none. Platform levelAccessWheelchair now
      maps to the Quay AccessibilityAssessment limitation LevelAccessIntoVehicle instead (same
      true/false/omit mapping as the old WheelchairAccess-labelled platform boolean below).

  xmllint schema-validity fixes (NeTEx_publication.xsd, v2.0):
  11. AccessibilityAssessment now always starts with mandatory MobilityImpairedAccess
      (AccessibilityAssessmentGroup): the WheelchairAccess limitation's value when present,
      "unknown" otherwise (flagged for business review; not triggered in this file, every
      AccessibilityAssessment here has a real WheelchairAccess/LevelAccessIntoVehicle-derived
      value).
  12. SanitaryEquipment: AccessibilityAssessment now written before SanitaryFacilityList
      (SanitaryEquipmentGroup order), not after.
  13. AssistanceService fields reordered to AssistanceFacilityList then AssistanceAvailability
      (AssistanceServiceGroup order; no Note/assistanceCondition text exists for these two
      stations, so Note is absent).
  14. StopPlace child order corrected to the Site/SiteElement/StopPlace XSD group sequence:
      Name, PrivateCode, Centroid, AccessibilityAssessment, placeEquipments, localServices,
      TransportMode, StopPlaceType, quays (no Url/PostalAddress exist for these stations).
-->
